From 6ecde5a8d15efbd7404041bf46413a7d70dc2643 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 17:24:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] prose_chip: Haiku's coding style, and nothing else

Includes in the guidelines' groups, alphabetical within each; C++ comments
rather than blocks, and doc comments that close on their own line; C++ casts --
static_cast from void*, reinterpret_cast between unrelated pointers, so the
safe ones are still checked -- and an operator that starts a wrapped line
rather than ending one.

No change in behaviour. The goto-based cleanup in prch_init_driver() stays: the
guidelines say avoid rather than never, it is how Haiku's drivers unwind a
partial initialisation, and changing it here would be a change of logic in a
change of style.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Prose-Patch: 0125-prose-chip-haiku-s-coding-style-and-nothing-else.patch 4a18fc3dd709070e6e0944ac47ca9536c3b3aa326fd18e0625959a087d5fcf15
